Description: screenshot tool with instant annotation
 ScreenCatch captures a region of the screen and opens it straight in an
 editor, so you can mark it up with arrows, rectangles, ellipses, lines,
 freehand pen and highlighter strokes, text and numbered steps, or pixelate
 sensitive details, before copying it to the clipboard or saving it as PNG.
 .
 It works on Wayland and X11 through the XDG desktop screenshot portal and
 registers a global keyboard shortcut (Ctrl+Shift+Print) on GNOME.
